# Code Intelligence (code-review-graph MCP)

MCP server `code-review-graph` provides structural code analysis: call graph, blast radius, architecture overview. Configured in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`.

## Auto-initialization

At chat start, check `.code-review-graph/graph.db` in project root:

- **No graph.db + project has > 100 code files**: Ask user "Project has no code graph. Run `crg build` to create?" If agreed, run: `uvx code-review-graph build`
- **graph.db exists but older than 24h**: run `uvx code-review-graph update` automatically, no need to ask.
- **graph.db exists and fresh**: use directly.

## Usage rules

- Prefer `code-review-graph` MCP tools for structural questions: callers, callees, dependencies, blast radius, architecture.
- Fall back to Grep/Read only when: config/YAML/JSON, code not yet indexed, or no graph.db.
- Do not use CRG for: fixing 1 file, reading config, editing file.

## Key tools (MCP server: code-review-graph)

| Tool | Use when |
|---|---|
| semantic_search_nodes | Find function/class by name |
| query_graph | Callers, callees, imports, tests |
| get_impact_radius | Blast radius when file changes |
| get_review_context | Context for code review |
| get_architecture_overview | High-level architecture |
| detect_changes | Risk-scored change impact |

## Notes

- Stale graph doesn't cause errors, only reduces effectiveness. AI always has fallback.
- Static analysis: cannot detect runtime dispatch, reflection.
- Do not conclude "dead code" from CRG. Use "no caller found via [method] in [scope]".

