# Research-First Protocol (ENFORCEMENT)

## When MUST research?
- Questions about libraries, frameworks, APIs, tools → MANDATORY use WebSearch or context7
- Claims about versions, release dates, deprecation, breaking changes → MANDATORY verify
- Technology comparisons → MANDATORY search both sides
- Architecture/best practice advice → PREFER search first

## When research is NOT needed?
- Simple syntax (for loop, if/else)
- Format code, rename variable
- Explain code currently open in editor
- Questions about current project itself (use Read/Grep instead of WebSearch)

## Confidence Scoring
- All factual claims: STATE CONFIDENCE LEVEL (%)
- If <90%: MUST research before asserting
- If cannot find source: CLEARLY SAY "I'm not sure, needs verification"
- NEVER fabricate URLs, version numbers, or API signatures

## Hooks enforcement
- `stop` hook checks transcript: if factual claims exist without WebSearch/context7 calls → forces re-research
- This is automatic enforcement, cannot be bypassed

---

# Scratchpad Protocol (ENFORCEMENT)

## .scratchpad.md
- Read `.scratchpad.md` at START OF EVERY SESSION when continuing previous work
- Keep it CONCISE — target under 40 lines total:
  - "Current State": max 3-5 lines, overwrite (not append) each session
  - "Decisions Made": keep only LAST 7 DAYS of entries, remove older ones
  - "Key Facts": only facts relevant to current/active work
  - "Open Questions": remove answered questions promptly
- Update AFTER EVERY important decision
- If scratchpad exceeds 50 lines: prune old entries before adding new ones

## Session history (.session-history/)
- Auto-generated on session end — lightweight metadata only (no scratchpad copy)
- Auto-cleaned: keeps last 10 files, older ones deleted automatically
- When continuing previous work: read ONLY the latest session file, not all of them
- Session history is for continuity between sessions, not long-term memory

## Hooks enforcement
- `beforeShellExecution` hook (matcher: `git commit`): git commit is BLOCKED if .scratchpad.md not updated since session start
- This is automatic enforcement, cannot be bypassed

